    "background_story": "Terry was a free-spirited artist who lived life on his own terms. He rejected the conventional norms of society, often embracing unconventional and unscientific methods to fuel his creativity. Terry believed that the universe held secrets that couldn't be explained by science, and he spent his days exploring the mysteries of the unknown. He dabbled in astrology, tarot reading, and other forms of mysticism, using these practices as inspiration for his art. Despite his unscientific approach to life, Terry's paintings were highly sought after for their unique energy and emotional depth. His friends and fans adored him for his quirky perspective, and Terry remained true to himself, never compromising his artistic vision to conform to the rational world.",
